  ],
  "cleared": false,
  "why_they_stand": "Both warnings are what single precision makes of the double-precision loft body: the stage holds exactly the float32 cast of v2-loft-s025.npz. ZeroAreaFaceChecker sees 996 faces whose float32 cross product is zero; usd-cad-summary.json counts 35 because it measures them in double. All 996 are caps, three distinct corners nearly on one line. WeldChecker sees 1,058 groups of identical float32 points; 1,056 are distinct in double, at most 7.3e-6 mm apart where the float32 spacing is 7.6e-6 mm, and 2 coincide in double, where the solid touches itself. Deleting the faces would open the surface and welding points that share no edge would pinch it. Three repairs that keep the surface closed were tried under a tolerance of 1e-4 mm fixed beforehand; none removes both warnings, because the flat faces come in chains across shared edges and 51 point groups lie on parts of the surface that are two or more edges apart. The stage is therefore left byte for byte as recorded. usd-validation-nvidia 1.23.0, alone in its venv, reports the same two warnings and nothing else on part.usda and part.usdz",
